  "title": "The life of a record",
  "subtitle": "A producer hashes the record's key to a partition and sends it to that partition's leader broker, which appends to an on-disk commit log and replicates to the follower replicas that live on the other brokers (the ISR). Every broker leads some partitions and follows others. A consumer group splits the partitions across its members; the KRaft controller holds cluster metadata. The thick path is the produce to a leader.",
